    duration: "15–20 min",
    hook: "Addiction is not about weakness of character or moral failure — it's about the brain's reward and learning systems being hijacked by powerful stimuli that override normal decision-making. Understanding addiction scientifically — how it develops, why certain people are more vulnerable, and what actually works to prevent and treat it — is one of the most important things you can know. Because the adolescent brain is specifically more vulnerable to addiction than the adult brain, and the choices you make now about substance exposure have permanent consequences.",
